  <text>
    <body>
      <p>Little Pelham Street is a narrow street running between <ref target="civic?id=Leicester%20Street">Leicester Street</ref> and <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref>, just north of <ref target="civic?id=Pelham%20Street">Pelham Street</ref>.</p>
      <p>It is first listed in the directories in 1869. It is missing from the 1875 to 1877 directories, and then listed in every directory up to 1940, the last one transcribed so far.</p>
      <div>
        <head>Along the street</head>
        <p>From 1905 the directories list the houses on its north side, starting from the Bouverie Street end and finishing at Leicester Street.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Businesses and landmarks</head>
        <list rend="bulleted">
          <item>National Motor Reconditioning Pty Ltd (1930) and the Rhodes Motor Co. (1935).</item>
          <item>A. C. Hatrick Pty Ltd, merchants, at Nos 16 to 24 (1940).</item>
        </list>
        <p>In 1930 one house, No. 28, is listed only as "Italians".</p>
      </div>
    </body>
